<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Berthold V, Duke of Zähringen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1218">1218</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Berthold V was the last duke of Zähringen, a powerful dynasty of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/switzerland">Switzerland</a>, ruling from 1186 to 1218. He founded the city of Bern in 1191 to strengthen his hold on the lands between the Jura and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a>, and declined the German crown offered to him in 1198. With his death in 1218 the main Zähringen line died out.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/berthold-v-duke-of-zahringen.jpg" alt="Berthold V, Duke of Zähringen" width="276" height="295" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Franz Zell · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Berthold_IV,_Duke_of_Z%C3%A4hringen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
